From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000002 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Keystone P550 Integration <keystone-p550@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] sm: allow P550 test platform without a device root key

The VF2 branch deliberately skips root-key copying on VisionFive 2. Apply the
same test-only behavior to the new P550 platform until a real device root of
trust is designed and provisioned.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [test-only board port]
---
 src/sm.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/sm.c b/src/sm.c
index d072e26..a2b421b 100644
--- a/src/sm.c
+++ b/src/sm.c
@@ -143,6 +143,6 @@ void sm_init(bool cold_boot)
     // Copy the keypair from the root of trust
     // Dont supported on visionfive2 for now
-    #ifndef BOARD_VISIONFIVE2
+    #if !defined(BOARD_VISIONFIVE2) && !defined(BOARD_P550_TEST)
     sm_copy_key();
     #endif
 
-- 
2.34.1
